[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Performance harness/configuration, size reports, and test
[stderr] +  matrix documentation; initial paths `scripts/release-check.*`, test config,
[stderr] +  `docs/{quality-plan,test-matrix}.md`.
[stderr] +- **Environment contract:** Configuration distinguishes public build metadata
[stderr] +  from development-only values, is typed and validated, and produces immutable
[stderr] +  candidate/version metadata. Development, test, and release procedures must
[stderr] +  identify the resolved non-secret configuration and toolchain version without
[stderr] +  printing secret values.
[stderr] +- **Performance contract:** Measure initial load, bundle/cache size, warm and
[stderr] +  offline startup, interaction/frame-time behaviour, memory, and feasible
[stderr] +  slow-network behaviour only against an approved browser/device/network
[stderr] +  matrix and numeric budget. Until that approval, collect measurements as
[stderr] +  informational evidence only; do not label them budget passes or make public
[stderr] +  performance promises.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Configuration positive/negative tests, artifact
[stderr] +  hash and size report, and measurement transcript tied to the candidate,
[stderr] +  browser/device/network profile, cache state, and method. Real-device,
[stderr] +  lab, paid-provider, or production measurements require the authorised
[stderr] +  executor's evidence and remain `not run` when unavailable.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Exact browser/device matrix, network profiles, numeric
[stderr] +  budgets, test hardware, runner/provider, and release performance threshold.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Documentation and quality contracts
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-06 — Player, operator, and authoring documentation
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** `docs/{player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,
[stderr] +  security-and-provenance,quality-plan,test-matrix,release-runbook,rollback,
[stderr] +  content-authoring}.md` and corresponding in-app Help/Status copy.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Player documentation explains controls, keyboard/touch/gamepad
[stderr] +  alternatives, saving/resume/delete/recovery, offline/first-install limits,
[stderr] +  update/cache status, accessibility settings, privacy/diagnostics choices,
[stderr] +  version/support path, and known limitations. Operator documentation defines
[stderr] +  release evidence, hold conditions, rollback, issue ownership, and
[stderr] +  compatibility declarations. Content guidance requires original-asset/text
[stderr] +  provenance and validation before bundling. Documentation must state
[stderr] +  unresolved browser, locale, assistive technology, performance, and support
[stderr] +  decisions instead of promising them.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Contract-to-document review checklist with
[stderr] +  candidate ID and reviewer; link checks; help/status UI review; provenance
[stderr] +  inventory review. Legal, accessibility, rating, store, translation, or
[stderr] +  support approval is not implied by a documentation check and requires its
[stderr] +  authorised reviewer record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-07 — Quality review and issue disposition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Deterministic/unit/content/persistence integration suite,
[stderr] +  browser evidence, manual matrix, release evidence register, and issue
[stderr] +  disposition template.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Quality evidence maps every release requirement to a method,
[stderr] +  candidate, result, artifact, and owner. Required layers are: deterministic
[stderr] +  core/content tests; persistence/migration/recovery fault injection;
[stderr] +  app/integration tests; supported-browser automated smoke for start, first
[stderr] +  battle, save/resume, recovery and PWA lifecycle where applicable; and manual
[stderr] +  responsive/accessibility/offline/storage checks after the matrix is approved.
[stderr] +  Test fixtures use isolated synthetic storage and never modify player data.
[stderr] +- **Issue rules:** A failing, blocked, missing, stale-candidate, or unverifiable
[stderr] +  required check is a release hold. Each known issue records severity, player
[stderr] +  impact, affected target, reproduction, mitigation, owner, and release
[stderr] +  decision. Only an explicitly authorised risk acceptance may waive a
[stderr] +  non-critical issue; it records approver, expiry, rationale, mitigation, and
[stderr] +  rollback trigger. Critical security, data-loss, save-corruption, privacy,
[stderr] +  or unbounded execution findings cannot be waived by this contract.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** CI-equivalent transcript; browser report;
[stderr] +  completed manual matrix; issue register; and an evidence freshness review
[stderr] +  confirming artifacts belong to the release candidate. Missing approvals or
[stderr] +  unavailable targets are recorded as holds, not manufactured passes.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Release readiness gate
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-08 — Evidence-based release or hold decision
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The release owner completes this gate for one immutable candidate. This record
[stderr] +does not grant deployment authority; it determines whether the candidate is
[stderr] +ready to be presented for an authorised release decision.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Gate | Required evidence | Hold when |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Candidate identity and compatibility | Version/build hash; content/save schema versions and supported ranges; known-good rollback target | Identity, hash, compatibility, or rollback target is missing or incompatible. |
[stderr] +| Trust and privacy | QOR-01 artifact secret scan/configuration result; QOR-02 consent/redaction/input-safety results; provenance/dependency review | A secret finding, unsafe parser/rendering result, missing consent/redaction evidence, or unresolved provenance/dependency risk exists. |
[stderr] +| Health and recovery | QOR-03 recovery evidence; QOR-04 save/migration/quarantine/cache-retention tests and rollback dry run | A fault lacks a safe path, save/recovery test fails, or rollback/recovery evidence is absent. |
[stderr] +| Quality and accessibility | QOR-07 CI/browser/manual evidence, with approved target matrix and all required contract mappings | A required check is fail, blocked, not run, stale, or lacks reviewable evidence. |
[stderr] +| Performance and environment | QOR-05 validated configuration, hash/size report, and approved-matrix measurement against approved budget | Required environment/budget/matrix evidence is unapproved, absent, or over budget without authorised disposition. |
[stderr] +| Documentation and known issues | QOR-06 review; player/operator material; issue register and any authorised, unexpired exception | Documentation is inaccurate/missing, an issue is undisposed, an exception is expired/unauthorised, or a non-waivable issue exists. |
[stderr] +| Authorised decision | Named release authority records `release` or `hold`, time, candidate, evidence links, and rationale | No authorised decision exists. An agent or automated check cannot substitute for this record. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Decision algorithm:** Record `HOLD` if any gate is held, any required evidence
[stderr] +is not real and candidate-specific, or an unresolved decision gate affects the
[stderr] +release claim. Record `READY FOR AUTHORISED RELEASE DECISION` only when every
[stderr] +applicable gate has passing evidence and no unwaivable issue. The authorised
[stderr] +release authority then records either `RELEASE` or `HOLD`; absent that record,
[stderr] +the outcome remains `HOLD / awaiting authority`.
