[stderr] +# 08 — Quality, operations, and release authoring contracts
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Inputs:** [delivery map](05-delivery-map.md), [foundation and domain
[stderr] +contracts](06-foundation-domain-contracts.md), [feature and experience
[stderr] +contracts](07-feature-experience-contracts.md), and the
[stderr] +[technical contract](../specification/03-technical-contract.md).
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Purpose and operating boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +These records turn the approved P0 trust, quality, recovery, and release
[stderr] +requirements into implementation contracts. They apply to the static,
[stderr] +client-side, offline single-player web/PWA release. They do **not** authorise
[stderr] +a server, account identity, remote saves, multiplayer, moderation, live
[stderr] +operations, analytics, purchases, entitlements, or an external crash-reporting
[stderr] +service.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`Evidence` means a reviewable artifact produced by the named check or a human
[stderr] +record with its date, release candidate version, executor, outcome, and any
[stderr] +exception. A generated report, screenshot, or command transcript may not be
[stderr] +invented, backdated, reused for a different candidate, or marked passing when
[stderr] +the underlying action did not run. Manual, external, paid, privileged, or
[stderr] +production actions remain `not run` until a named authorised person supplies
[stderr] +real evidence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Paths are planned implementation paths until the framework and tooling are
[stderr] +approved. A later runbook must cite the applicable contract IDs and must stop
[stderr] +at an unresolved decision gate rather than silently selecting a provider,
[stderr] +browser matrix, budget, retention period, or production process.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Shared evidence record
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Each record used for a release has this minimum metadata:
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Field | Required content |
[stderr] +| --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Candidate | Immutable build/version identifier and content/save-schema compatibility declaration. |
[stderr] +| Requirement | Contract ID and exact requirement or check being evidenced. |
[stderr] +| Method | Command, test name, manual procedure, or approved external system used. |
[stderr] +| Result | Pass, fail, blocked, or not run; failures link to an issue or explicit hold. |
[stderr] +| Evidence location | Immutable log/report/artifact path or authorised reviewer record. |
[stderr] +| Executor and time | Person or CI identity and actual completion timestamp. |
[stderr] +| Exceptions | Approver, expiry, risk, mitigation, and rollback trigger; empty when none. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +No release gate may infer a pass from missing fields. CI may attest only to the
[stderr] +checks it actually executed. An agent may prepare commands, templates, and
[stderr] +evidence tables, but may not claim a production deployment, payment,
[stderr] +third-party scan, account action, manual device test, legal review, or approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Trust and privacy contracts
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-01 — Secret, configuration, and authorization boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Build configuration schema, example configuration,
[stderr] +  release-time secret scan, and security documentation; initial paths are root
[stderr] +  configuration, `.secrets.env.example`, `scripts/release-check.*`, and
[stderr] +  `docs/security-and-provenance.md`.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Client artifacts contain only public, validated release
[stderr] +  metadata. Required configuration fails closed when absent or malformed.
[stderr] +  Credentials, private keys, tokens, service credentials, and `.secrets.env`
[stderr] +  are never committed, bundled, logged, copied into examples, or supplied to
[stderr] +  test fixtures. Secret-like findings block release until removed, revoked if
[stderr] +  exposure is confirmed, and rescanned; an agent cannot perform revocation or
[stderr] +  assert it occurred.
[stderr] +- **Authorization:** P0 has no server resource or identity boundary and hence
[stderr] +  has no application roles to implement. Browser-profile access is not an
[stderr] +  authorization guarantee. Any future endpoint, remote state, diagnostic
[stderr] +  transport, or privileged operation is prohibited until a separate approved
[stderr] +  contract specifies authenticated per-request authorization, least privilege,
[stderr] +  rate limiting, audit events, consent, deletion/retention, incident owner,
[stderr] +  outage behaviour, and real production evidence.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Positive and negative configuration tests;
[stderr] +  client artifact secret scan; dependency/lockfile review; CSP/static-header
[stderr] +  configuration review after a host is approved. Store command output and the
[stderr] +  scanned candidate identifier. A host header capture is `not run` before an
[stderr] +  authorised deployment exists.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Engine/build tool, hosting/CDN, CSP/header mechanism,
[stderr] +  dependency policy, and any connected service.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-02 — Privacy, diagnostics, and safe input handling
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Local diagnostics policy and redaction tests in
[stderr] +  `src/{app/recovery,platform/web/diagnostics}`, plus
[stderr] +  `docs/privacy-and-recovery.md`.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** P0 persists only local campaign state, preferences, bounded
[stderr] +  recovery metadata, and a player-controlled bounded diagnostic record. It
[stderr] +  does not collect names, contact data, precise location, advertising IDs,
[stderr] +  account identifiers, payment data, or gameplay analytics. Diagnostics have
[stderr] +  no network transport in P0, are off where consent is required, state their
[stderr] +  fields/purpose/retention/deletion locally, and exclude credentials, complete
[stderr] +  saves, free-text dialogue, and player-entered content.
[stderr] +- **Input trust:** Content packages, save imports if later approved, URL
[stderr] +  parameters, browser events, service-worker messages, and persisted bytes are
[stderr] +  untrusted. Bound size before parse, validate schema/references/checksum, do
[stderr] +  not execute authored data as code, and never render dialogue through unsafe
[stderr] +  HTML. Invalid input fails safely without overwriting a confirmed save.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Consent-default, redaction, clear-record,
[stderr] +  hostile/malformed payload, size-bound, and unsafe-rendering tests. A manual
[stderr] +  privacy-copy review records the candidate and reviewer. Any external privacy
[stderr] +  review, legal assessment, data export, or transport test is `not run` unless
[stderr] +  separately approved and evidenced by its authorised owner.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Retention period, legal/age/regional policy, export
[stderr] +  workflow, and every non-local diagnostic capability.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Operations and resilience contracts
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-03 — Local observability, health, and player recovery
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Development structured logs, release/version/cache status,
[stderr] +  error boundary, and local fault records; initial paths
[stderr] +  `src/{app/recovery,platform/web/diagnostics,platform/web/pwa}` and support
[stderr] +  UI/help copy.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Observability is local and player-respecting: development
[stderr] +  console/build logs, visible release/version/cache state, and optional bounded
[stderr] +  local diagnostics. Production P0 has no remote health endpoint, telemetry
[stderr] +  dashboard, pager, or monitoring dependency. The health signal is therefore
[stderr] +  a reproducible client verification, not a claim that a deployed service is
[stderr] +  healthy.
[stderr] +- **Recovery behaviour:** An unexpected fault presents `Retry`, `Return to
[stderr] +  title`, and `Safe recovery`, places focus on the actionable summary, avoids
[stderr] +  replaying a stale destructive command, preserves confirmed progress, and
[stderr] +  keeps quarantined data untouched absent confirmed deletion. Every error,
[stderr] +  storage, cache, or content failure has a player-facing path and a test for
[stderr] +  retained save/cache behaviour.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Fault-injection and recovery state-machine
[stderr] +  tests; browser evidence for the injected-fault flow; a recorded inspection
[stderr] +  of version/cache/support status. Before a production host is approved,
[stderr] +  production availability monitoring and incident response exercises are
[stderr] +  explicitly `not run`.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Hosting, support owner/response expectation, external
[stderr] +  monitoring, and diagnostics transport.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-04 — Save integrity, migration, rollback, and recovery
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Save protocol, migration runner, cache-release rollback
[stderr] +  procedure, and recovery documentation; initial paths
[stderr] +  `src/{core/save,core/session,platform/web/persistence}`, `docs/rollback.md`,
[stderr] +  and `docs/release-runbook.md`.
[stderr] +- **Migration contract:** Save and content schemas declare explicit versions
[stderr] +  and supported predecessor ranges. Migrations are ordered, pure, and promote
[stderr] +  only a validated candidate; each supported predecessor fixture migrates once.
[stderr] +  A failed or unsupported migration preserves original bytes in quarantine and
[stderr] +  offers a clear fallback/new-game path. No agent may alter a real player save
[stderr] +  to prove migration or recovery.
[stderr] +- **Rollback contract:** A rollback selects a previously verified, immutable
[stderr] +  known-good release compatible with the declared save/content ranges. It must
[stderr] +  not delete, rewrite, migrate, synchronise, or claim to restore player saves.
[stderr] +  Service-worker activation remains at title or paused menu after a confirmed
[stderr] +  save; failed refresh retains the known-good cache. Rollback is held if
[stderr] +  compatibility, cache retention, or recovery evidence is absent.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Fault-injection tests for interrupted write,
[stderr] +  malformed snapshot, quota/permission failure, quarantine, deletion, and
[stderr] +  migration; dry run against a synthetic fixture profile; recorded prior-build
[stderr] +  identifier, compatibility declaration, procedure output, and reviewer.
[stderr] +  A production rollback is never simulated or claimed without deployment
[stderr] +  authority and independently captured evidence.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Storage API/quota, support retention policy, service
[stderr] +  worker rollout, hosting rollback mechanism, and supported schema window.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-05 — Performance and environment measurement contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Performance harness/configuration, size reports, and test
[stderr] +  matrix documentation; initial paths `scripts/release-check.*`, test config,
[stderr] +  `docs/{quality-plan,test-matrix}.md`.
[stderr] +- **Environment contract:** Configuration distinguishes public build metadata
[stderr] +  from development-only values, is typed and validated, and produces immutable
[stderr] +  candidate/version metadata. Development, test, and release procedures must
[stderr] +  identify the resolved non-secret configuration and toolchain version without
[stderr] +  printing secret values.
[stderr] +- **Performance contract:** Measure initial load, bundle/cache size, warm and
[stderr] +  offline startup, interaction/frame-time behaviour, memory, and feasible
[stderr] +  slow-network behaviour only against an approved browser/device/network
[stderr] +  matrix and numeric budget. Until that approval, collect measurements as
[stderr] +  informational evidence only; do not label them budget passes or make public
[stderr] +  performance promises.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Configuration positive/negative tests, artifact
[stderr] +  hash and size report, and measurement transcript tied to the candidate,
[stderr] +  browser/device/network profile, cache state, and method. Real-device,
[stderr] +  lab, paid-provider, or production measurements require the authorised
[stderr] +  executor's evidence and remain `not run` when unavailable.
[stderr] +- **Decision gates:** Exact browser/device matrix, network profiles, numeric
[stderr] +  budgets, test hardware, runner/provider, and release performance threshold.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Documentation and quality contracts
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-06 — Player, operator, and authoring documentation
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** `docs/{player-guide,accessibility,privacy-and-recovery,
[stderr] +  security-and-provenance,quality-plan,test-matrix,release-runbook,rollback,
[stderr] +  content-authoring}.md` and corresponding in-app Help/Status copy.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Player documentation explains controls, keyboard/touch/gamepad
[stderr] +  alternatives, saving/resume/delete/recovery, offline/first-install limits,
[stderr] +  update/cache status, accessibility settings, privacy/diagnostics choices,
[stderr] +  version/support path, and known limitations. Operator documentation defines
[stderr] +  release evidence, hold conditions, rollback, issue ownership, and
[stderr] +  compatibility declarations. Content guidance requires original-asset/text
[stderr] +  provenance and validation before bundling. Documentation must state
[stderr] +  unresolved browser, locale, assistive technology, performance, and support
[stderr] +  decisions instead of promising them.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** Contract-to-document review checklist with
[stderr] +  candidate ID and reviewer; link checks; help/status UI review; provenance
[stderr] +  inventory review. Legal, accessibility, rating, store, translation, or
[stderr] +  support approval is not implied by a documentation check and requires its
[stderr] +  authorised reviewer record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-07 — Quality review and issue disposition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / owns:** Deterministic/unit/content/persistence integration suite,
[stderr] +  browser evidence, manual matrix, release evidence register, and issue
[stderr] +  disposition template.
[stderr] +- **Contract:** Quality evidence maps every release requirement to a method,
[stderr] +  candidate, result, artifact, and owner. Required layers are: deterministic
[stderr] +  core/content tests; persistence/migration/recovery fault injection;
[stderr] +  app/integration tests; supported-browser automated smoke for start, first
[stderr] +  battle, save/resume, recovery and PWA lifecycle where applicable; and manual
[stderr] +  responsive/accessibility/offline/storage checks after the matrix is approved.
[stderr] +  Test fixtures use isolated synthetic storage and never modify player data.
[stderr] +- **Issue rules:** A failing, blocked, missing, stale-candidate, or unverifiable
[stderr] +  required check is a release hold. Each known issue records severity, player
[stderr] +  impact, affected target, reproduction, mitigation, owner, and release
[stderr] +  decision. Only an explicitly authorised risk acceptance may waive a
[stderr] +  non-critical issue; it records approver, expiry, rationale, mitigation, and
[stderr] +  rollback trigger. Critical security, data-loss, save-corruption, privacy,
[stderr] +  or unbounded execution findings cannot be waived by this contract.
[stderr] +- **Verification / evidence:** CI-equivalent transcript; browser report;
[stderr] +  completed manual matrix; issue register; and an evidence freshness review
[stderr] +  confirming artifacts belong to the release candidate. Missing approvals or
[stderr] +  unavailable targets are recorded as holds, not manufactured passes.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Release readiness gate
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### QOR-08 — Evidence-based release or hold decision
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The release owner completes this gate for one immutable candidate. This record
[stderr] +does not grant deployment authority; it determines whether the candidate is
[stderr] +ready to be presented for an authorised release decision.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Gate | Required evidence | Hold when |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Candidate identity and compatibility | Version/build hash; content/save schema versions and supported ranges; known-good rollback target | Identity, hash, compatibility, or rollback target is missing or incompatible. |
[stderr] +| Trust and privacy | QOR-01 artifact secret scan/configuration result; QOR-02 consent/redaction/input-safety results; provenance/dependency review | A secret finding, unsafe parser/rendering result, missing consent/redaction evidence, or unresolved provenance/dependency risk exists. |
[stderr] +| Health and recovery | QOR-03 recovery evidence; QOR-04 save/migration/quarantine/cache-retention tests and rollback dry run | A fault lacks a safe path, save/recovery test fails, or rollback/recovery evidence is absent. |
[stderr] +| Quality and accessibility | QOR-07 CI/browser/manual evidence, with approved target matrix and all required contract mappings | A required check is fail, blocked, not run, stale, or lacks reviewable evidence. |
[stderr] +| Performance and environment | QOR-05 validated configuration, hash/size report, and approved-matrix measurement against approved budget | Required environment/budget/matrix evidence is unapproved, absent, or over budget without authorised disposition. |
[stderr] +| Documentation and known issues | QOR-06 review; player/operator material; issue register and any authorised, unexpired exception | Documentation is inaccurate/missing, an issue is undisposed, an exception is expired/unauthorised, or a non-waivable issue exists. |
[stderr] +| Authorised decision | Named release authority records `release` or `hold`, time, candidate, evidence links, and rationale | No authorised decision exists. An agent or automated check cannot substitute for this record. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Decision algorithm:** Record `HOLD` if any gate is held, any required evidence
[stderr] +is not real and candidate-specific, or an unresolved decision gate affects the
[stderr] +release claim. Record `READY FOR AUTHORISED RELEASE DECISION` only when every
[stderr] +applicable gate has passing evidence and no unwaivable issue. The authorised
[stderr] +release authority then records either `RELEASE` or `HOLD`; absent that record,
[stderr] +the outcome remains `HOLD / awaiting authority`.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Retained decisions and excluded actions
[stderr] +
[stderr] +1. Engine/framework, package manager, CI runtime, storage API/quota, host/CDN,
[stderr] +   service-worker rollout, browser/device/assistive-technology matrix,
[stderr] +   performance budgets, locales, retention policy, legal/age/regional policy,
[stderr] +   and support ownership require approval.
[stderr] +2. Production hosting, deployment, rollback execution, external scans, paid
[stderr] +   test services, real-device labs, store submission, legal review, and any
[stderr] +   account action require separately granted authority and real evidence.
[stderr] +3. Account identity, cloud sync, multiplayer/player safety, live-service
[stderr] +   operations, analytics, commerce, and entitlements remain excluded. They
[stderr] +   need new product, privacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode
[stderr] +   contracts before implementation or release claims.
